{"id":"17704b001a890a71","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-df-zfc-recursive-projective-hierarchy-level.md","title":"ZFC Recursive Projective Hierarchy Level","display":"df-zfc-recursive-projective-hierarchy-level — ZFC Recursive Projective Hierarchy Level","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-recursive-projective-hierarchy-level","aliases":["58-df-zfc-recursive-projective-hierarchy-level"],"display":"df-zfc-recursive-projective-hierarchy-level — ZFC Recursive Projective Hierarchy Level","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","[[58-df-zfc-lightface-projective-set.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-omega.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-recursive-projective-hierarchy-level"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-recursive-projective-hierarchy-level</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-recursive-projective-hierarchy-level — ZFC Recursive Projective Hierarchy Level"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md\">../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"e1021998813b00da\" href=\"?note=e1021998813b00da\" title=\"58-df-zfc-lightface-projective-set.md\">58-df-zfc-lightface-projective-set.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5045d216c83e75cb\" href=\"?note=5045d216c83e75cb\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-omega.md\">../batch16/58-df-omega.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,X,n\\in V\">\\(A,X,n\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcRecursiveProjectiveHierarchyLevel}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcRecursiveProjectiveHierarchyLevel}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma^{1,\\emptyset}_n,\\Pi^{1,\\emptyset}_n\\subseteq\\mathcal P(\\omega^\\omega)\">\\(\\Sigma^{1,\\emptyset}_n,\\Pi^{1,\\emptyset}_n\\subseteq\\mathcal P(\\omega^\\omega)\\)</span> (lightface projective pointclasses, as used by <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"e1021998813b00da\" href=\"?note=e1021998813b00da\" title=\"58-df-zfc-lightface-projective-set.md\">58-df-zfc-lightface-projective-set.md</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}recursive\\text{-}projective\\text{-}hierarchy\\text{-}level}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcRecursiveProjectiveHierarchyLevel}_S(A,X,n)\\leftrightarrow\nX=\\omega^\\omega\\land n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land\nA\\subseteq X\\land\n\\bigl(A\\in\\Sigma^{1,\\emptyset}_n\\lor A\\in\\Pi^{1,\\emptyset}_n\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}recursive\\text{-}projective\\text{-}hierarchy\\text{-}level}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcRecursiveProjectiveHierarchyLevel}_S(A,X,n)\\leftrightarrow\nX=\\omega^\\omega\\land n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land\nA\\subseteq X\\land\n\\bigl(A\\in\\Sigma^{1,\\emptyset}_n\\lor A\\in\\Pi^{1,\\emptyset}_n\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The earlier definition passed pointclass symbols to a predicate whose second argument is a class of formula codes.  This version uses the lightface pointclasses directly and records their Baire-space carrier.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md","status"